; panchaavayava: the five-limbed proof structure from nyaya.
; every answer the system produces follows this structure:
; pratijna (thesis) → hetu (reason) → udaharana (example) → upanaya (application) → nigamana (conclusion)
;
; the emit layer implements this:
; emit-pratijna ("we have") → emit-hetu ("we seek") → emit-udaharana-upanaya ("we know/see") → emit-nigamana ("we find")
;
; the structure is not imposed — it arises from the graph walk:
; pratijna reads what is given, hetu reads what is sought,
; udaharana walks the mantra edges, upanaya substitutes values,
; nigamana reads the derived result.

(sangati panchaavayava
  (swarupa nyaya)
  (sthita pramana-sthalam)
  (yukta pratijnaa hetu udaharana upanaya nigamana)
  (kriya pramana)
  (phala anuvada)
  (siddha parampara))
